**The weekly app report, not a problem: nothing needs doing.** ${log.extracted_label.period}.

- **Estimated net revenue:** ${log.extracted_label.revenue}
- **Purchases:** ${log.extracted_label.purchases}
- **Model spend:** ${log.extracted_label.spend}
- **Estimated margin:** ${log.extracted_label.margin}
- **Recipes:** ${log.extracted_label.recipes}
- **Free recipes:** ${log.extracted_label.free}
- **Refunds:** ${log.extracted_label.refunds}
- **Problems:** ${log.extracted_label.problems}

Changes against the week before are in brackets. Every figure is the server's own estimate, the owner board's arithmetic: revenue is `netMicroUsdPerCredit` per recipe sold, net of refunds, never a store payout; spend is worked out from token counts, never the Cloud bill. The full report and the last weeks: ${log.extracted_label.console} (card "Weekly report"), or `npm run admin -- report weekly --project <id>`.

Sent by the Monday job `weeklyPromptReview` (`weekly_report_ready`; `weekly_report_failed` when the report could not be made, and then "Problems" says why and how to run it again). It is an alert policy only because alerts are how the backend emails the owner: severity WARNING, the lowest. To stop these emails, disable this policy in Cloud Monitoring (Alerting > Policies), or set `enabled` to false in functions/alerts/policies/weekly-report.json and apply it; to stop the report itself, turn off "Make and email the weekly report" on the owner console. functions/README.md, "Weekly app report".
